# GameHoverDetails: preview vs hover parity

When editing **GameHoverDetails** hover UI or settings preview:

- **`HoverFieldListBuilder.Fill`** is the **single** field-list visual tree. **`GameHoverDetailsHoverService`** owns fingerprint, width, chrome, frost, and placement, then calls `Fill` with `HoverFieldListSource.ForLiveGame` (`OmitEmptyArt = true`). **`GameHoverDetailsSettingsView`** XAML only wraps preview chrome (`PreviewChromeBorder`, fanart, tint, dim-when-disabled). Field rows go in **`PreviewFieldsHost`** (`StackPanel`) via the same `Fill`.
- **Preview source** — `OmitEmptyArt = false` so missing Icon/Cover/Background fall through to sample text (a normal text row). Art still uses the settings cache / fallback library icon. Values use `HoverFieldFormatter` then `HoverPreviewSampleText` when the library game has no data. Platform icons come from the sample game when present.
- **Titles** — Game-art keys (`HoverFieldCatalog.IsGameArtImageField`: Icon, Cover Image, Background Image) have **no** title row (`TryAppendGameArtRow`). Do not add titles for those keys in a parallel preview path.
- **Icon-only** — When **Icon** is the **only** selected field and the bitmap loads, the builder shows **Name** beside the 40 DIP icon (`onlyIconSelected`); text uses `VerticalAlignment="Center"` next to the image.
- **Columns** — `HoverFieldColumnCount` (1–3, default 1) packs non-spanning fields left-to-right, then down. **Cover Image**, **Background Image**, and **Description** always span the full inner width (flush the current row first). Empty omitted-art slots do not leave a hole — the next field fills that cell. One-column mode keeps the original stacked separators and insets.
- **Icons** — Inline catalog glyphs (Phosphor / Unicons / Huge Icons via `HoverIconStyle`) sit in a chip column sized by `HoverIconChipOuterSizeDip` (size + 2× padding; default chip **32** DIP) with **10** DIP gap to text when `ShowFieldInlineIconsInHover` and the field is **not** game-art. Glyph size is `HoverIconGlyphFontSize`. Chip corners come from `HoverIconChipShape` (`ResolveIconChipCornerRadius`). `HideIconChipBackground` makes `HoverChromePalette.GlyphChipBackground` transparent (glyph only). With icons off, body is full width — no reserved empty column.
- **Stat row** — When titles and inline icons are both on, one grid row: chip | stacked label + value (`ConfigureFieldLabelTextBlock` + body). Do not put a full-width title above the chip for that mode.
- **Separators** — `AppendFieldBlockSeparator` uses `SeparatorPadDip` (0.5× block spacing) and **`HoverChromePalette.Separator`**. `HideFieldDividers` drops the 1px line (`Height` 0) but keeps the spacer margins. Last-block bottom inset is always trimmed (`TrimLastContentBottomMargin`).
- **Description** — Plain text only: `HoverDetailValuePresenter.HtmlToPlainText` then the existing **3-line** `FormattedText` clamp + ellipsis. No HTML inlines, bold, or links (hover dismisses when the pointer enters the panel).
- **Fanart chrome** — Paint overview art with an **`ImageBrush`** on a stretch `Border` (`PreviewCoverHost` / hover `coverHost`). Never put a layout-participating `Image`/`Canvas` in the chrome — that made the panel as tall as the bitmap. Frost snapshots use a **non-measuring overlay** around the `Image` for the same reason (last capture height must not stick after fields are removed). `Stretch.UniformToFill` crops overflow (typically the sides). Height follows the field list.
- **Width** — Preview and live hover both use `HoverWidth` (`ResolveHoverPanelWidth()`). Do not scale fanart wider than the slider, and do not cap the preview at 216/280.
- **Settings** — Keep preview chrome in sync with `HideFieldTitlesInHover`, `ShowFieldInlineIconsInHover`, `HideIconChipBackground`, `HideFieldDividers`, `HidePanelBorder`, `HoverChromeDividerHex`, `HoverBodyFontSize` / `HoverTitleFontSize` (line heights `18/13` and `14/10.5`), `HoverIconStyle` / `HoverIconChipSizeDip` / `HoverIconChipPaddingDip` / `HoverIconChipShape`, `HoverFieldColumnCount` / `HoverFieldBlockSpacingDip` / `HoverContentPaddingDip`, `UseGameBackground` / `HoverBackgroundStyle` (overview fanart + opacity-scaled #000000 tint; height follows the field list; fanart `Stretch.UniformToFill` covers the panel while keeping aspect ratio), `HoverChromeBackgroundOpacity`, `UseThemeChrome` / custom chrome (`HoverChromePalette`), and inner width relative to `HoverWidth` (`HoverContentPaddingDip` on each side; hover inset is **2×** that). Fanart must still cover the panel edge-to-edge under that padding (clip to the 8 DIP corner radius).

See **`src/GameHoverDetails/AGENTS.md`** (Preview vs hover parity) for the canonical checklist.
